## Metadata
Title: FUN'S Cross-Word Puzzles
Author: Ernest A. Grant
Copyright: New York World
Date: 1914-06-21
Number: 24
Notes: A 13-wide diamond with a cross-shaped centre block printed "No 24" (r5c7, r6c6-c8, r7c5-c9, r8c6-c8, r9c7; shown as _), so the middle column holds two short words (33-34 VISE above the block, 35-36 FLEE below). Number printed in the centre block ("No 24") and in the intro ("the twenty-fourth in FUN'S series"); the heading is "FUN'S CROSS-WORD PUZZLES Can You Solve Them?". Credit as printed in the intro: "Today's cross word puzzle, the twenty-fourth in FUN'S series, is contributed by Ernest A. Grant of Washington, D. C." Read by hand from the Milwaukee Sentinel's page (Milwaukee_Sentinel_1914_06_21_87.png), solution from Milwaukee_Sentinel_1914_06_28_74.png, by Claude, 2026-11-16.


